     3. The recovery module extracts a controlled amount of mechanical energy (prioritizing deceleration, descent gliding, or high-entropy exhaust/wake regions).
     4. The electrical generator converts mechanical rotation into raw electrical power.
     5. Power electronics regulate the voltage/current for onboard avionics.
     6. The Intelligent Energy Management System decides in real time whether recovered power is routed to sensors/avionics or battery storage, or bypassed during climb/acceleration to minimize drag.
